        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "The current behavior is actually easier to deal with, since the events fired after `:edit` and `:checktime` is different: \r\n\r\n```\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:15.559 DEBUG (pid:13727) [model-document] - buffer detach\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:15.560 DEBUG (pid:13727) [index] - Autocmd: BufUnload\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:15.579 DEBUG (pid:13727) [index] - Autocmd: FileType\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:15.587 DEBUG (pid:13727) [index] - Autocmd: BufCreate\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:15.611 DEBUG (pid:13727) [index] - Autocmd: BufEnter\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:15.624 DEBUG (pid:13727) [index] - Autocmd: TextChanged\r\n```\r\n```\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:21.434 DEBUG (pid:13727) [index] - Autocmd: BufCreate\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:21.455 DEBUG (pid:13727) [index] - Autocmd: FileType\r\n2018-06-27T16:01:21.466 DEBUG (pid:13727) [index] - Autocmd: TextChanged\r\n```\r\nThere's no `BufUnload` nad `buffer detach` for `:checktime`, so I could just update the content when `BufCreate` fired for existing buffer.",
