        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "So imho the behavior between `edit` and `checktime` needs to be consistent. How about:\r\n\r\n- `edit <otherfile>`: send `nvim_buf_detach_event`\r\n- `edit` aka `edit <thesamefile>`: send `nvim_buf_lines_event` with the full new buffer data (we probably can't just send a diff here reasonably, can we?)\r\n- `checktime` with no reload: do nothing\r\n- `checktim` with reaload: sent `nvim_buf_lines event` with the full new buffer data\r\n\r\nThis seems to mesh well with the \"least surprise\" approach. Anyone thinking that's not the right thing to do? One thing to think about is the changedtick, but I guess that's solveable.\r\n\r\nI'd work on it, but I'm not sure I can do it without some hand-holding, in particular wrt the conditions we need to test this under.",
