        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@KillTheMule  makes sense to me.\r\n\r\n> `edit` aka `edit <thesamefile>`: send `nvim_buf_lines_event` with the full new buffer data (we probably can't just send a diff here reasonably, can we?)\r\n\r\nThis is yet another case where comparing a hash of the file contents would be useful.  Before unloading a buffer, Nvim could hash the contents. Then _while_ loading a buffer, it's a small cost to compute a hash of the contents.  Of course, this doesn't avoid the reload, but at least Nvim could avoid nagging the user in some cases--and avoid resending the entire buffer in the above case.",
